CORE
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
__builtin_constant_p must recognise integer constant arithmetic as constant for
both GCC and Clang, irrespective of the operator (subtraction, division,
modulo, shifts, ...). Run under the ansi-c-clang profile this exercises the
Clang-specific constant-folding path, which previously only handled addition
and multiplication and so wrongly reported e.g. __builtin_constant_p(1 - 1) as
non-constant.
